            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Mold and mildew can grow on dust, cardboard, wood and fabric whenever relative humidity stays above roughly 60 percent, even without visible water. The musty odor is the gas they release. Measure the humidity with a hygrometer; if it is high, a dehumidifier set to 45 to 50 percent and removing cardboard and old carpet usually clears the smell within weeks."
