          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What humidity should a basement be?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The EPA recommends keeping indoor relative humidity below 60 percent and ideally between 30 and 50 percent. For a basement in summer, 45 to 50 percent is a practical target that limits mold and dust mites without running a dehumidifier around the clock. Readings above 60 percent for long stretches are when musty smells and mildew start."
          }
