          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Dampness itself is not dangerous, but the mold and dust mites it supports can aggravate allergies and asthma, and long-term moisture can rot wood framing. If anyone in the house has respiratory problems, or if there is visible mold over about 10 square feet, address it promptly. Testing for radon is also wise in any basement, damp or not."
