          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What causes chalky white deposits on concrete walls?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is efflorescence, mineral salts carried through the concrete or block by water and left behind when the water evaporates. It is harmless itself but it is a sign that moisture travels through the masonry. Sweep it away with a dry stiff brush, fix outdoor drainage, and if it keeps returning, clean the wall and apply a masonry waterproofer or penetrating sealer."
          }
        },
